<title>MEXICO: Mexico revises June coffee export data downward.</title>
<headline>Mexico revises June coffee export data downward.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico exported 148,009 60-kg bags of coffee in June compared to the 193,292 bags in June last year, the Mexican Coffee Council said Monday.</p>
<p>The figures are a downward revision of previous preliminary export data. The council originally said exports in June were 151,661 bags.</p>
<p>A full breakdown of updated Mexican exports follows in table form for the country's October-September cycle. Figures are for 60-kg bags.</p>
<p>    Month	  1996-1997	   1995-1996</p>
<p>    October	 163,489	     101,912</p>
<p>    November	320,842	     296,510</p>
<p>    December	390,111	     421,445</p>
<p>    January	 871,321	     745,428</p>
<p>    February	837,812	     742,815</p>
<p>    March	   671,570	     631,513</p>
<p>    April	   447,980	     529,015</p>
<p>    May	     270,214	     458,195</p>
<p>    June	    148,009	     193,292</p>
<p>    July		N/A		 219,432</p>
<p>    August	    N/A		 146,745</p>
<p>    September	 N/A		  92,554</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530))</p>
